    "id": "SHIFT_AVNG_L2_temporal_mosaics_2289_1",
    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "This dataset contains mosaicked surface reflectance from imagery acquired by NASA's Airborne Visible / Infrared Imaging Spectrometer-Next Generation (AVIRIS-NG) instrument. This imagery was collected as part of the Surface Biology and Geology High-Frequency Time Series (SHIFT) campaign over California, U.S., in 2022. Gridded mosaic files are available for 13 separate days of flights during 2022-02-24 to 2022-05-29. The SHIFT campaign leveraged NASA's AVIRIS-NG facility instrument to collect VSWIR data at approximately a weekly cadence across a broad study area, enabling traceability analyses related to the science value of VSWIR revisits. AVIRIS-NG is a pushbroom spectral mapping system with high signal-to-noise ratio (SNR), designed and toleranced for high performance spectroscopy. AVIRIS-NG measures radiance at approximately 5-nm intervals in the Visible to Shortwave Infrared (VSWIR) spectral range from 380-2510 nm. Surface reflectance, derived from AVIRIS-NG radiance, was georeferenced, atmospherically and topographically corrected, and normalized for 9 to 12 flight lines then combined to produce a mosaic for each date. Reflectance in 425 bands and 5-m resolution is provided in ENVI format in tiles covering 6.23 km x 5.46 km. The dataset includes a full resolution RGB image in GeoTIFF format for each date and an index map of image tiles in GeoJSON format.",
